# Testing

## All tests

- Two Vitest runners (D-12): `web` uses `@angular/build:unit-test`; libraries use `@nx/vitest`. Do not migrate either.
- Stub timers with `vi.useFakeTimers()` only. No `fakeAsync` / `tick` (zoneless, D-10).

## Angular (apps/web)

- Await render with `await fixture.whenStable()`.
- Set signal inputs via `fixture.componentRef.setInput()`.
- Assert behaviour through the DOM, not private component fields or methods.

## Libraries

- Vitest does not type-check. After changing library code or specs, run `npx nx run <lib>:typecheck` (D-13).
- TDD for `plate-domain`: see `AGENTS.md`.
- `plate-domain` enforces 100% lines and branches (D-18): an uncovered branch fails `test`. Cover it with a test — never with an ignore hint or a coverage exclusion.

## E2E (apps/web-e2e)

- Locators: `getByRole`, `getByText`, `getByLabel`. No CSS selectors, no `waitForTimeout`.
- Prefer web-first assertions (`await expect(locator).toHaveText(…)`).
- Chromium only for now (D-14).
- E2E may import `@plate-region/plate-data` to assert real regions (D-06).
